  "plain": "In the 1950s, the story goes, the American researcher Thomas Townsend Brown moved among powerful men such as the physicist Edward Teller and the Air Force general Curtis LeMay, and was often driven home in a black Cadillac by a man his daughter, Linda Brown, later came to know as Robert Sarbacher. Michels tells it in his own summary, crediting the book The Man Who Mastered Gravity by Paul Schatzkin and Linda Brown's memory of the car and its driver. If true, it would put Brown close to the inner circle of postwar weapons science."
